---

description: Performance rules for bullet-hell gameplay
globs: ["wipshmup2/scripts/**/*.gd", "wipshmup2/shaders/**/*.gdshader"]
alwaysApply: true
---

# Object Pooling
- Reuse bullet/enemy instances; toggle `visible` instead of `queue_free()` where applicable.
- Cleanup via factory; disconnect signals before reusing.

# Rate Limiting
- Respect MAX bullet counts and per-second caps; degrade gracefully when exceeded.

# Per-Frame Budget
- Avoid allocations in `_process/_physics_process`.
- Cache nodes/resources; pre-load where hot.
- Avoid unbounded loops; split work across frames if needed.

# Math & Types
- Prefer integer-safe ops where relevant (e.g., bit-shift for halves in counts).

# Diagnostics
- When adding logs, gate them or keep them terse to prevent spam during bullet storms.